    {
      "file": "newsboat-runtime-2.45.tar.gz",
      "built_from": "Newsboat 2.45 source from https://newsboat.org/releases/2.45/newsboat-2.45.tar.xz; built on Ubuntu 24.04 with GCC 14 and Rust 1.94.0 using cargo fetch --locked and make newsboat. The binary is stripped and its RPATH set to $ORIGIN/../lib. Ubuntu shared libraries are copied, stripped and assigned a local library search path; pbsandbox.so is compiled from the accompanying pbsandbox.c. Component package/source versions are in notes."
    }
  ],
  "modifications": "No upstream Newsboat source changes. Binary stripping and RPATH changes; a separate LD_PRELOAD library applies filesystem and process restrictions.",
  "configuration": "HOME and the working directory are DATA_DIR. The runtime supplies a local starter subscription. Newsboat uses its native configuration; Landlock confines data access to the instance and terminal devices, and seccomp disables execution of external programs. Local feed files and an offline loopback feed server are available.",
  "notes": {
    "source": {
      "url": "https://newsboat.org/releases/2.45/newsboat-2.45.tar.xz",
      "version": "2.45",
      "sha256": "defe303d2518f3c4241780a9165e8750e9984e3f10aa341b7dde107579e34b3d"
    },
    "build": {
      "base_image": "ubuntu:24.04@sha256:68ee22004a9109b44973313b02ff7b1de250f1de0f5ecb628d73f579aaff33ac",
